  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There should be an option in the menu to enable auto alignment for avatars that will try and force the avatar into a t-pose. Some avatars might be placed into an awkward pose when calibrating, with the legs spread and rotated, spine bent, neck hunched, arms lowered, as well as have viewpoints that may not be accurately placed on the avatar that may affect movement of the head and center of the body. This option will forcefully align body components so they stay as centered and in the correct pose as possible, and point as straight as possible, along with some level of viewpoint correction which may be disabled. This will help adapt many avatars to work better with FBT, even if the creator has not, is unwilling, or is unable to test, update, or fix the pose.",
